From 70056bc10b57b6c519c16d67c8048b2be0d23bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:24:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: installd restores an app's data in two steps (stage,
 then commit or abort)

stageTreeTarZst extracts into a staging dir and writes a done marker last; commitStage swaps it in
only when the marker is there; abortStage removes it. The one-call restore is stage + commit. The
staging names count as caches so a backup never archives them and a swap never clears them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
